     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and many guidelines use 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney function.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. Possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg three times daily** or **1000 mg twice daily**, which are common regimens.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, which could be split into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If you really do intend 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
